For an intent \(I\), host \(H\), and policy \(P\), select an admitted realization from a feasible set:

\[
R^* \in
\operatorname{ParetoMin}_{R\in\mathcal F(I,H,P)}
\bigl(
\text{authority},
\text{trusted surface},
\text{operational cost},
\text{maintenance burden},
\text{latency}
\bigr).
\]

The feasible set carries the correctness obligations. Optimization happens inside it.
