- Contract changes carry compatibility and migration obligations.
- Assumptions have owners and invalidation conditions.
- Acceptance records identify which checker and policy admitted a release.
- Emergency changes can run under constrained, explicitly provisional status.
- Revocation identifies affected deployments and dependent claims.
- Retirement removes operational code without deleting the evidence needed to understand prior decisions.

A real institution can explain not merely “why did CI pass?” but:

> Why was this behavior authorized, on this host, with these effects, under these assumptions—and who could change those terms?

