## What gdp-wired actually is

It's an automatic prover for stateful rules — budgets, caps, rate limits, workflows, access policies — where you write the rule (params, inputs, state, step) plus the laws it must keep, and a call like `proveRule` proves them with no hand-written proof. When a law is false, a GPU search finds a concrete breaking run from the start state; every proof tree is checked by a small trusted kernel, and the kernel has a proven-sound twin in Lean 4.34.0 that re-checks the real trees. Untrusted parts (the CDCL/prove search, GPU synthesizer, runtimes) are held to the trusted kernel: if they're wrong, the kernel rejects the tree. They're also pushing toward gdp-ts integration, where a trusted module proves its laws at load time and then mints per-call-site proof tokens that every caller is held to. [github](https://github.com/monotykamary/gdp-wired)

